IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `theft-nouns`

-- Theft Act 1968, section 34: interpretation. Layer 1.
--
-- Section 34(1) carries ss 4(1) and 5(1) to the whole Act. In this encoding every
-- offence that needs a theft calls `s 1 guilty of theft`, which calls both, so no
-- separate rule is needed for 34(1); NOTES.md says which sections it matters to.
--
-- Section 34(2)(c) gives "mail bag" and "postal packet" the meanings in section
-- 125(1) of the Postal Services Act 2000, which is not among the inputs, so whether
-- a thing is one is a fact the person states (`Mail facts`, s 14).

§ `Section 34 - interpretation`

-- src:262 | (1) Sections 4(1) and 5(1) of this Act shall apply generally for purposes of this Act as they apply for purposes of section 1.
-- src:263 | (2) For purposes of this Act—
-- src:264 | (a) “gain” and “loss” are to be construed as extending only to gain or loss in money or other property, but as extending to any such gain or loss whether temporary or permanent; and—
-- src:265 | (i) “gain” includes a gain by keeping what one has, as well as a gain by getting what one has not; and
-- src:266 | (ii) “loss” includes a loss by not getting what one might get, as well as a loss by parting with what one has;
-- src:267 | (b) “goods”, except in so far as the context otherwise requires, includes money and every other description of property except land, and includes things severed from the land by stealing ; and.
-- src:268 | (c) “mail bag” and “postal packet” have the meanings given by section 125(1) of the Postal Services Act 2000.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 34 (src:262-268)
GIVEN g IS A `Gain or loss facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(2)(a) a view to gain or an intent to cause loss` g MEANS
        (    g's `he had a view to gain for himself or another`
         AND g's `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property`)
    OR  (    g's `he intended to cause loss to another`
         AND g's `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property`)

-- s 34(2)(b). "Goods" includes money and every other description of property except
-- land, and includes things severed from the land by stealing.
@ref Theft Act 1968 s 34(2)(b) (src:267)
GIVEN t IS A `Goods facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(2)(b) the thing is goods` t MEANS
    NOT (t's `they are land, or a thing forming part of land that has not been severed from it by stealing`)
